      en: "Icheon Ceramics Village in Icheon city, South Korea, is a hub for traditional Korean ceramic production. The village hosts over 300 ceramic workshops and 50 galleries. Icheon is renowned for its high-quality pottery, especially Icheon celadon and white porcelain (baekja). The tradition dates back to the Joseon Dynasty (1392–1910). The annual Icheon International Ceramics Festival attracts over 1 million visitors. The city also operates a ceramics museum. Workshops offer hands-on pottery lessons. Ceramics are exported to over 30 countries.",
